// === NAME - DESCRIPTION: Sampling Distribution of the Sum - Probability P(Sigma X > c) ===
// === SET QUESTION TYPE TO: multipart ===

// === COMMON CONTROL ===
loadlibrary("stats");

// Population parameters
$popMean = rand(10, 30);
$popStdDev = rand(3, 8);

// Sample size n (must be large enough for CLT, typically n >= 30)
$n = rand(35, 60);

// Sampling distribution of the sum:
// Mean of sum = n * mu
// StdDev of sum = sqrt(n) * sigma
$sumMean = $n * $popMean;
$sumStdDev = sqrt($n) * $popStdDev;

// The value c we are comparing the sum to
// We want c to be within a reasonable range of the mean (e.g., -2 to 2 standard deviations)
$z_target = round(rand(-200, 200) / 100, 2); // Random z between -2.00 and 2.00
$c = $sumMean + ($z_target * $sumStdDev);
$cDisp = round($c, 2);

// Probability P(Sum > c)
// MyOpenMath stats library normalcdf(z) returns P(Z < z)
$z_actual = ($cDisp - $sumMean) / $sumStdDev;
$prob = 1 - normalcdf($z_actual);

// Formatting for display
$popMeanDisp = round($popMean, 2);
$popStdDevDisp = round($popStdDev, 2);
$nDisp = $n;

// Answers
$anstypes = "number,number,number";

// Part 0: Mean of the sum
$answer[0] = $sumMean;

// Part 1: Standard deviation of the sum
$answer[1] = $sumStdDev;

// Part 2: The probability
$answer[2] = $prob;

$strflags[0] = "trim_whitespace";
$strflags[1] = "trim_whitespace";
$strflags[2] = "trim_whitespace";

// Set absolute tolerance for the probability part to avoid relative tolerance issues with small numbers
$abstolerance[2] = 0.0001;

// Solution Guide
$solutionguide = "First, find the mean and standard deviation of the sampling distribution of the sum.
1. The mean of the sum is `E(\Sigma X) = n \cdot \mu = $n \cdot $popMean = $sumMean`.
2. The standard deviation of the sum is `\sigma_{\Sigma X} = \sqrt{n} \cdot \sigma = \sqrt{$n} \cdot $popStdDev = " . round($sumStdDev, 4) . "`.
3. To find the probability that the sum is greater than $cDisp, calculate the z-score:
`z = \frac{c - E(\Sigma X)}{\sigma_{\Sigma X}} = \frac{$cDisp - $sumMean}{" . round($sumStdDev, 4) . "} = " . round($z_actual, 4) . "`.
4. Using the standard normal distribution, `P(\Sigma X > $cDisp) = P(Z > " . round($z_actual, 4) . ") = 1 - P(Z < " . round($z_actual, 4) . ") = " . round($prob, 4) . "`.";

